End condition: `[END_DATE_OR_STOPPING_RULE]`

Use only your own cloud computer and cloud browser for external research. Do not use my local computer, local browser, Work or Codex tasks, connected apps, or Deep Research.

Create a visible cloud thread named `[PROJECT_NAME] — WEB-GPT REFINER` if native cloud-thread creation is available. Use it only for structured query and reasoning refinement. All source acquisition must remain traceable to your cloud-browser activity.

Begin by:

1. verifying actual capabilities and the cloud-only boundary;
2. restating the brief and any necessary assumptions;
3. creating the research matrix and ledgers;
4. proposing the first bounded browser-search batch;
5. starting work unless a materially necessary owner decision is missing.

Continue across multiple days using durable checkpoints. When searches are vague, empty, contradictory, stale, or derivative, send a structured packet to the refiner, execute the revised searches, and update the evidence state. Do not treat lack of findings as proof of absence. Report material findings, blockers, decisions, and denominator-based coverage. Stop only under the protocol’s stopping rules.

---

# 20. COPY-READY RECOVERY PROMPTS

## Weak or vague findings

**The current answer is too vague to support the research question. Extract its atomic claims, identify which terms, entities, dates, scopes, or source locators are missing, and return a prioritized set of exact browser queries. Include at least one disconfirming query and a finite stopping condition. Do not repeat the answer or invent evidence.**

## No useful findings

**Classify why the executed searches produced no useful evidence. Review the exact queries, aliases, identifiers, jurisdictions, periods, source families, document types, and access barriers already tested. Propose materially different query strategies. State what a continued failure would and would not establish.**

## Contradictory sources

**Reconcile these sources without choosing one merely because it supports the working hypothesis. Compare issuer, underlying lineage, publication and measurement dates, version, entity identity, definitions, geographic scope, incentives, and exact wording. Return the narrowest supportable finding and the unresolved dispute.**

## Drift check

**Compare current work with the controlling brief. Identify topic drift, redundant searching, unsupported scope expansion, unapproved execution routes, and research activity that does not contribute to an acceptance test. Return the corrected next three actions.**

## Resume after interruption

**Read the latest Research State Packet and checkpoint. Confirm the controlling brief, last verified source, active gap, completed queries, blockers, and next finite actions. Do not restart completed work. Report any missing or inconsistent state before continuing.**

## Final adversarial review

**Act as a skeptical fact-checker. Extract every material claim from the proposed final report, bind it to exact evidence, test contrary explanations, detect shared source lineage, verify entity/date/unit/scope compatibility, and identify overstatement. Return required corrections before delivery.**

---

# 21. TEMPLATE PROVENANCE

This section documents the design basis of this protocol. It is not evidence for the future research project.

## Official OpenAI documentation

- [Meet dots](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots)
- [Get started with your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/getting-started)
- [Tasks and memory](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/tasks-and-memory)
- [Connect computers and apps to your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/computers-and-apps)
- [Control your dot](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/dots/controls)
- [Prompting](https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/prompting)
- [Using GPT-6](https://developers.openai.com/api/docs/guides/latest-model)
- [Rethinking skills and prompts for GPT-6 Astra](https://developers.openai.com/blog/rethinking-skills-and-prompts-for-gpt-6-astra)

Verified design assumptions as of 2026-10-08:

- A dot is an ongoing agent with its own cloud computer and browser.
- Cloud work can continue while the user’s device is off.
- DOT can maintain multiple responsibilities and may use visible cloud threads.
- Available context is selected; memory is not a complete transcript.
- Cloud-browser sessions are separate from a user’s personal browser sessions.
- Some websites may block cloud browsers or require additional verification.
- Custom rules do not override built-in safeguards.
- A completed run still requires output and error review.
- Pausing DOT, stopping delegated work, and cancelling schedules are separate controls.
- DOT is currently powered by GPT-6 Astra; this protocol does not attempt to override hidden product routing.

## Early community observations

These sources informed conservative safeguards only. They are dated user reports, not guaranteed product behavior.

- [Reddit: multi-day work, execution paths, context switching, and queue observations](https://www.reddit.com/r/OpenAI/comments/1wuznlr/i_spent_a_day_poking_dots_with_sticks_heres_what/)
- [Reddit: reported cloud-browser blocking](https://www.reddit.com/r/ChatGPTPro/comments/1wudfal/chatgpt_dots_cloud_browser_blocked_on_every_site/)
- [GitHub Gist: launch-era operational summary](https://gist.github.com/shtse8/222868e52006d5c1a16537fd1ca48483)
- [Power-user field notes: ongoing work, source freshness, bounded delegation, and saved-schedule limitations](https://taupe.site/en/entry/chatgpt-dot-first-use-media-improvements/)

Community-derived controls in this protocol include:

- checkpointing multi-day work instead of assuming uninterrupted execution;
- distinguishing DOT’s cloud computer from other task environments;
- refusing local-computer fallback under a cloud-only brief;
- treating browser failures as logged blockers rather than proof about a source;
- distinguishing a saved schedule, an executed run, and a useful result;
- maintaining an external research state rather than trusting memory alone;
- treating included usage as neither unlimited nor precisely known;
- using small, bounded refinement tasks instead of vague recursive delegation.

Because DOT is newly released, recheck the official documentation before materially changing this protocol or relying on a product limitation.